utions, hemodialysis concentrates, solutions and granulates, bloodlines, renal pharmaceuticals, systems for water treatment, and acute cardiopulmonary and apheresis products. In addition, the company develops, acquires, and in-licenses renal pharmaceuticals; offers renal medications and supplies to patients at homes or to dialysis clinics; and provides vascular specialty, ambulatory surgery center, physician nephrology practice management, pharmacy and other services. The company sells its products to dialysis clinics, hospitals, and specialized treatment clinics, as well as through local sales forces, independent distributors, dealers, and sales agents. The company was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Bad Homburg, Germany.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shervin J. Korangy | CEO & Chairman of the Management Board | Age 51 | Compensation: $280,855 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 106K people. Revenue per employee of $204K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Fresenius Medical Care AG is a large-cap healthcare business with a $11.4B market cap on $21.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 31%.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 9.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (44% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 26% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Valued at a 47% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Focus Graphite (CVE:FMS) Shares Up 1.5% \u2013 Still a Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/focus-graphite-cvefms-shares-up-1-5-still-a-buy.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794550396.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"We Like Fresenius Medical Care's (ETR:FME) Earnings For More Than Just Statutory Profit","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/de/healthcare/etr-fme/fresenius-medical-care-shares/news/we-like-fresenius-medical-cares-etrfme-earnings-for-more-tha